Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Cold Tallow Chokes the Rewind Crank
- Story & Context: Janusz broke his left thumb during a freezing December shift at the ruined Roxy Cinema in Bytom when the manual film winder seized up in a basin of congealed mutton fat he had used for gear lubricant. Refusing to go to the hospital, he strapped his bloody hand to a battered Les Paul and hammered out this inaugural track while Ewa pinned down the 909 kick to 215 BPM, creating a storm of noise that blew out the venue's remaining glass chandeliers while he screamed into the horn, "The feast never had a face, but the fire eats anyway."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A brutally stark macro photograph of a rusted iron film winder caked in white, solidified animal lard and severed brown film ribbons, illuminated by the harsh incandescent glare of an inspection lamp on a grease-blackened workbench; floating dust and grain; an abrasive, industrial still life with cold, sorrowful textures.

Track 2: "Who Salted This Silver Broth?"
- Story & Context: In the pitch-black crawlspace behind Screen 3, Ewa wept into an enamel bowl of steaming cabbage broth as she spliced together five minutes of blank film, mourning her sister who had emigrated twenty years prior without leaving a single photograph. Between sobbing verses sung through a megaphone, she attacked an undamped snare drum with an iron meat tenderizer to puncture the soaring, melancholic hard-rock arpeggios, whispering into the microphone just before the gabber kick dropped: "Pass the bitter broth to whoever isn’t here."
